    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0673" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-15T14:00:00+02:00">March 15, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 15—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Rumanian Legation informs me that it granted transit visa without stopover on
                    consular registration and identity certificate to Insull this morning and that
                    it expects him to arrive at Constanza on Polish flag vessel <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Polonia</hi> leaving Piraeus tomorrow, March 16th.
                    Rumanian Legation understands that fugitive’s destination is Poland via
                    Tcheko-slovakia. Owsley<anchor n="33" xml:id="d478-f1"/> here asks you inform
                        Holmes<anchor n="34" xml:id="d478-f2"/> unless already done.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d478-f1" n="33" xml:id="d478-f1-content">
                <p>Alvin M. Owsley, Minister in Rumania.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d478-f2" n="34" xml:id="d478-f2-content">
                <p>Julius Cecil Holmes, Third Secretary of Legation in Rumania.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
